{{Quote|Echo Base, this is Rogue Two. I've found them. Repeat, I've found them.|Zev Senesca, after locating Luke Skywalker and Han Solo on Hoth|<ref name="ESB" />}}
'''Zev Senesca''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[rebel pilot]] who served the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] as a founding member of [[Rogue Squadron]]. While operating on [[Hoth]], Senesca flew a [[T-47 airspeeder|snowspeeder]] under the [[callsign]] [[Rogue Two]]. He was the [[pilot]] who located the missing Alliance members [[Captain]] [[Han Solo]] and [[Commander]] [[Luke Skywalker]], and he later participated in the [[Battle of Hoth]]. During the battle, Senesca and [[Kit Valent|his gunner]] [[Death|died]] when their snowspeeder was shot down by an [[All Terrain Armored Transport|AT-AT]].

==Biography==
===Early life===
{{Quote|Like hunting starwhales on Uthura! I'm coming home!|Zev Senesca, during the Battle of Hoth|<ref name="SYWTBAJ">''[[The Empire Strikes Back: So You Want to Be a Jedi?]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Zev-hd.png|thumb|left|250px|Zev Senesca locates Han Solo and Luke Skywalker.]]
Zev Senesca was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[Reproduction|born]] on the [[Kestic Station]] near the [[Bestine system]]. At some point, Senesca left Kestic Station<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> and resided on [[Uthura]], where he [[Hunting|hunted]] [[starwhale]]s.<ref name="SYWTBAJ" /> By the [[time]] of the [[Galactic Civil War]], Senesca had joined the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]], serving the [[Rebel Alliance Starfighter Corps]]. After joining the Alliance, he met [[Wedge Antilles]] and [[Derek Klivian|Hobbie]] whilst at one of [[General]] [[Hera Syndulla]]'s training exercises.<ref name="Star Wars 45">[[Star Wars (2015) 45|''Star Wars'' (2015) 45]]</ref>

===Mako-Ta===
In [[1 ABY]],<ref name="TImelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> Senesca was present at the [[Mako-Ta Space Docks]] when the [[Galactic Empire]] launched an [[Battle of Mako-Ta|assault]] on the Alliance's base. Whilst stuck aboard the<ref name="Star Wars 51">[[Star Wars (2015) 51|''Star Wars'' (2015) 51]]</ref> [[Star Cruiser]] [[Republic (MC80A Home One Type Heavy Star Cruiser)|''Republic'']]<ref name="Star Wars 55">[[Star Wars (2015) 55|''Star Wars'' (2015) 55]]</ref> Senesca told Klivian that he knew and accepted the risks of fighting the Empire.<ref name="Star Wars 51" /> Thanks to [[Han Solo]], the Rebel starfighters were eventually able to launch, and Senesca, serving as a founding member of [[Rogue Squadron]], flew an X-wing in the battle.<ref name="BuildXwing20">{{BuildXWingCite|20|Starfighter Aces}}</ref>

===Hoth===
{{Quote|Set for position three.|Zev Senesca shortly before being shot down|<ref name="ESB" />}}
In [[3 ABY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> Senesca was among the Rebels stationed at [[Echo Base]] on the [[Water|ice]]-[[planet]] of [[Hoth]], where he flew a [[T-47 airspeeder]] under the [[callsign]] of [[Rogue Two]].<ref name="ESB" /> Senesca organized a betting pool for the worst thing about their new base, which pilot [[Dak Ralter]] won for betting on "too damn cold." Senesca and his fellow pilots liked to fly the airspeeders, but they were not operational for some time due to the cold weather and the squadron were forced to use [[tauntaun]]s until the engineers were able to adapt their equipment.<ref name="FACPOV">{{StoryCite|story=Rogue Two (short story)|book=From a Certain Point of View: The Empire Strikes Back}}</ref>

[[File:ZevSenescaHS-TESB.png|thumb|right|250px|Senesca during the Battle of Hoth]]
When [[Rogue Leader]] [[Luke Skywalker]] went missing during a patrol, [[Captain]] Han Solo went in search of him. As news spread of their missing leader, Senesca, as the new first in command of Rogue Squadron, gathered the pilots in the barracks and started a new betting pool, saying the first Rogue pilot to find Skywalker would win a week's worth of wages off of his squadronmates. Ralter and [[Wedge Antilles]] wrote their names on the board, but when [[Derek Klivian|Derek "Hobbie" Klivian]] said that it was morbid, [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] walked in and said that she thought it was a gesture filled with hope and that she was confident they could find him. The entire squadron then entered the pool. The following morning, Senesca led Rogue Squadron and located the two missing [[officer]]s. Thinking of Organa's words, Senesca smiled to himself as he approached Solo and Skywalker, also remembering that he had won a lot of extra flight pay.<ref name="FACPOV" />

Soon after, the Galactic Empire discovered Echo Base, and the Rebel Alliance began an evacuation. During the subsequent [[Battle of Hoth]], Senesca piloted his snowspeeder,<ref name="ESB" /> with [[Kit Valent]] serving as his [[gunner]].<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> While defending Echo Base, Senesca's snowspeeder was hit by an Imperial [[All Terrain Armored Transport]] twice. The first shot damaged their snowspeeder enough to slow it down, making the second the killing strike that [[Death|killed]] both Senesca and Valent.<ref name="BuildXwing20" />

==Personality and traits==
Senesca was a brave rebel pilot and honorably served in multiple engagements during the Galactic Civil War. He did not enjoy life on Hoth, hating the snow and the cold wind, but nonetheless continued to serve. Senesca often organized betting pools for his squadron, including one about how long it would take General Organa to tire of Captain Solo's attempts to flirt and show off in front of her. Senesca did not hold Solo in the highest regard, thinking him to be a "blowhard" who had a big mouth and possessed more luck than talent. However, ultimately, Senesca respected Solo for being heroic and putting himself at risk to go search for Skywalker.<ref name="FACPOV" />

==Behind the scenes==
Zev Senesca was created for the [[1980]] film [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']], in which he was portrayed by actor [[Christopher Malcolm]]. The film's credits identified the character as "Zev (Rogue 2),"<ref name="ESB" /> and the surname of "Senesca" was later [[canon]]ized in ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]'', a [[2015]] reference book.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" />

According to ''Ultimate Star Wars'', Senesca hailed from Kestic Station.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> However, the 2015 junior novel ''[[The Empire Strikes Back: So You Want to Be a Jedi?]]'' states that Uthura is his [[homeworld]],<ref name="SYWTBAJ" /> and a cohesive timeline from [[Lucasfilm]] has yet to be determined.

The helmet used by Zev in the film was later used by an unidentified pilot in the ''[[Home One]]'' briefing room scene in [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="SW Costumes">''[[Star Wars Costumes: The Original Trilogy]]''</ref>

